# =============================================================================
# Phantom C2 — .gitignore
#
# Engagement loot (credential dumps, Kerberos ccaches, hives, ad-hoc exploit
# scripts) does not belong in this tree. It lives outside the repo at:
#
#     ~/engagements/<engagement>/
#
# Everything below is a safety net so an accidental `git add .` can never commit
# engagement data. If loot reappears at the repo root, treat that as a bug and
# move it out again rather than leaning on these rules.
#
# Patterns are anchored with a leading "/" when they are only meant to catch
# loose files dropped at the repo ROOT, so legitimate files in subdirectories
# (configs/, deployments/, docs/) are not silently swallowed.
# =============================================================================

# Binaries
build/
*.exe
*.out
*.bin
phantom-server
phantom-agent

# Database
data/*.db

# Runtime logs and sessions
logs/
*.log
*.rec

# Keys and certs
configs/*.pem
configs/*.key
configs/*.crt
*.pem
*.key

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Go
vendor/
*.test

# Loot and logs
loot/
configs/server.key
configs/.phantom_creds

# Environment / secrets — never commit
deployments/redirector/.env

# Lab/CTF artifacts — never commit
*.ccache
*.pvk
*.der
credman.txt
root.txt
root_ad_dump.txt
flag*.txt
f.txt
SECURITY
/config
puppet.conf
ed25519
ed25519.pub
dc01*
task_root.xml
.claude/

# Credential dumps & sensitive loot — NEVER commit (engagement data)
*.dmp
*.dit
ntds.dit
SAM
SYSTEM
*.restore
auth.csv
*.csv
authorized_keys
.ssh/
creds.txt
C:\\creds.txt
darkc0de_crack.log
sessions.txt

# Ad-hoc exploit / pentest scripts (repo root only — C2 code lives in cmd/ & internal/)
/*.py
/*.so
/*.sql
/*.ps1
/*.json
/dirty_cred_exp
/exp_file_credential
/pwnkit*
/hydra.restore
ScheduledTasks.xml
fd_watcher*.sh
nikto_*.txt
*ws77*

# Loose root-level text drops.
# The repo root tracks no .txt files, so this closes the whole class rather than
# blacklisting names one at a time. Added 2026-10-08 after ntlm.txt — a 33-byte
# credential dump — proved to be the single artifact the previous net missed.
/*.txt

# Local Tandem agent state (never commit)
.tandem/
